rked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=2$ and $y=-3.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have a strict inequality, we use dashed lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/6c1830847adf66b3d015227fb2b822d236cc0ca04d4e79b34485e0e307bebfb2.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/e04638efe40ea1813185855bb8c9a47e3e782487f6497ba63c7ed5e9046af421.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x-2)^{3}$ | $(y+3)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(1,-2)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(3,-2)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(1,-4)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(3,-4)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)>0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/51df420aa99597c5f476be571557aa9f1c91a1ec1f888687058bfd0fe96813e4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff63683317b1ff68128f81c27594160ddb5912a52e3945dd03e8f649d0905b33"} {"question" "q-121313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8535935689f512014d69f4f37d9eb2fb99191853e23ef5af94320df3ebeec9a"} {"question" "q-121313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff63683317b1ff68128f81c27594160ddb5912a52e3945dd03e8f649d0905b33"} {"question" "q-121313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/28d18defd0b2fbd2565e3929e0acf2575d9ecbe90e931a43e2806616e8041094.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/6979eefe00fcb6e1c0e7cb5b993d9b3e162922443d26a6571bd3a86679576d86.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/8180521b3a878e91950d27111104c0c2ef918ac67dd3ec902fc3861e56270179.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/b5f63ced598cd8a8a28f774b1d11cf73e340827b2032fd574bc7b9612e4ff467.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/b8f4397a5b7dea9e0cbad1c2e61f2a595658dbfad0ecee82e5797ed0431c8ca1.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff63683317b1ff68128f81c27594160ddb5912a52e3945dd03e8f649d0905b33"} {"question" "q-121313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/b5f63ced598cd8a8a28f774b1d11cf73e340827b2032fd574bc7b9612e4ff467.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff63683317b1ff68128f81c27594160ddb5912a52e3945dd03e8f649d0905b33"} {"question" "q-121310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)=(x+1)^{2}(y+2).$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\le 0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff63683317b1ff68128f81c27594160ddb5912a52e3945dd03e8f649d0905b33"} {"question" "q-121310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=-1$ and $y=-2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/26f786cb4b0e0d923502a6fef4c827341a5a8c5f61d497ec479742db3ee7ea87.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/0f68fc744e359192c65134f941952d8cfcf928b1f74924896df09ea23a36d07f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x+1)^{2}$ | $(y+2)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-2,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(0,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-2,-3)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(0,-3)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\le 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/206cc195b55db8f3793f4d84d0bd3b78f21430759770c8be4c815f8db8d562fb.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff63683317b1ff68128f81c27594160ddb5912a52e3945dd03e8f649d0905b33"} {"question" "q-121310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8535935689f512014d69f4f37d9eb2fb99191853e23ef5af94320df3ebeec9a"} {"question" "q-121310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff63683317b1ff68128f81c27594160ddb5912a52e3945dd03e8f649d0905b33"} {"question" "q-121310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/10080518e756d9d915dadc4346c23a9db90ff7d0f8df90b09f571b3f9f8aa29c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/74cb28a25b133ac6ce3b5abcccef89620350ca901fd60ec66888ed7fee454e18.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/91ec230c1251255ad019b445ba18bc35cf46ebf5fceaac74a359ecd819e5ec1d.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/d996ae0305472b14d52d3ec951669590aad2a249a3ce2f2643d65ad17993a899.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/ec94dbaaf4cc906de62faa9c2eea1ca9028915377f18ff5bf4aa5bd8d53b2df2.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "fil